{"senses": [{"examples": [{"text": "\"Do tell us the real name of your country, and then when you are gone we shall know how to talk about you.\" To this luminous argument and remonstrance I could oppose nothing but assertion, and the whole party remained firmly convinced that I was for some reason or other deceiving them.", "ref": "1869, Alfred Russel Wallace, The Malay Archipelago, volume II, London: Macmillan and Co., page 247:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[178, 187]]}], "links": [["assert", "assert"], ["positive", "positive"], ["declaration", "declaration"], ["averment", "averment"]], "categories": ["English terms with quotations"], "glosses": ["The act of asserting; positive declaration or averment."], "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "You're a man of strong assertions!", "bold_text_offsets": [[23, 33]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Suppose you are given the semifactual assertion, \"even if Nora had liked mathematics then she would have became^([sic]) a scientist\" and then you find out that Nora did in fact become a scientist.", "ref": "2007 January 26, Ruth M. J. Byrne, The Rational Imagination: How People Create Alternatives to Reality, MIT Press, →ISBN, page 140:", "type": "quotation", "bold_text_offsets": [[38, 47]]}], "synonyms": [{"word": "contention"}], "categories": ["English terms with quotations", "English terms with usage examples"], "glosses": ["Something which is asserted; a declaration; a statement asserted."], "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"]}, {"examples": [{"text": "That's just a bare assertion.", "bold_text_offsets": [[19, 28]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Drivers' union ASLEF bluntly rebuffed the claim of unofficial action, calling it a lie. And Avanti West Coast was unable to provide any proof for its assertion, when questioned by RAIL.", "ref": "2022 August 24, Philip Haigh, “Network News: Union slams Avanti West Coast: 'lie' as services slashed”, in RAIL, number 964, page 6:", "type": "q